{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106996","id":2556757201,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6YZQTR","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106996","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106996.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106996.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106996","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106996/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106996/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106996/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/963c20565b0652012468450ede6e8193c7be5657","number":106996,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Core: Remove `OAHashMap`, in favor of `AHashMap`","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- Motivated by https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12515\r\n\r\nWe have 5 similar [hashing containers](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/cpp_usage_guidelines.html) in Core. \r\nThis is confusing, because the trade-offs are [not clear](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12515). This PR removes `OAHashMap`, in favour of the nearly identical (but faster) `AHashMap`.\r\n\r\n## Comparison\r\n\r\nWhen `OAHashMap` was [first added](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/11405), it was the fastest hashing container, because it used round-robin probing and contiguous data allocations.\r\nSince then, `HashMap` [was reimplemented in 2022](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/60881) with round-robin probing, making it more competitive with `OAHashMap` again.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, `AHashMap` [was added in 2024](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/92554). It makes [nearly the same decisions](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12515) as `OAHashMap`. \r\nIt wasn't questioned back then, but because the two types make nearly the same decisions, `AHashMap` should have been a re-implementation of `OAHashMap`. Now, we have two nearly identical data types.\r\n\r\nThere's 3 notable differences, though:\r\n- `AHashMap` has an interface mostly consistent with `HashMap` (our most common hashing data type). `OAHashMap` has an inconsistent interface.\r\n- `OAHashMap`'s implementation is less well optimized than `AHashMap`'s (see benchmarks).\r\n- `OAHashMap` uses separate value and key arrays (discussed below).\r\n\r\nDue to these factors, I think it is appropriate to replace `OAHashMap` entirely, to alleviate our maintenance burden.\r\n\r\n## Dense `KeyValue` array vs sparse `Key` array + `Value` array\r\n\r\nThe only theoretical difference between `OAHashMap` and `AHashMap` is that `AHashMap` stores its values in one dense `KeyValue` array, while `OAHashMap` stores theirs in two separate, sparse arrays.\r\n\r\n- `AHashMap`'s `KeyValue` array can be iterated densely. Because the iteration is contiguous, it is fast. `OAHashMap` has to check every next value for 'aliveness' (40-80% success rate). In addition, it iterates the metadata array, the values array, and the keys array, making 3 separate memory accesses. Both of these factors make iteration very slow in comparison.\r\n- `AHashMap` `erase` has to make another lookup, to account for the relocated value. This makes it slower than `OAHashMap`'s erase. \r\n- `AHashMap`'s `insert` and `lookup` (usually) only needs two cache misses. `OAHashMap` usually needs three cache misses, making it slower for cold access.\r\n- `OAHashMap` needs to relocate values and keys on rehash. `AHashMap` only needs to re-insert metadata.\r\n- `OAHashMap` needs element arrays of full capacity. `AHashMap`'s KeyValue arrays need only be 75% of capacity, saving memory.\r\n- `AHashMap`'s `KeyValue` array may need padding, adding up to 7 bytes per element (`byte` key and `double` value). In this rare case, `AHashMap` will use more memory than `OAHashMap` (but less than 10% added memory). \r\n\r\nMost of the difference between the two decisions are in favour of `AHashMap`. Most notably, access and iteration are favourable for `AHashMap`. This makes it the better choice for most situations.\r\n\r\n## Benchmarks\r\n\r\nI tested insertion, updating, erasing and access on hot hash maps (cold maps are discussed above, but not tested).\r\nI found that `AHashMap` is favourable to `OAHashMap` in nearly all situations, often more than 5x.\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Test code</summary>\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nfor (int size : { 1, 2, 8, 64, 1024, 4096, 20000}) {\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tsize_t time_ns = 0;\r\n\t\t\tsize_t time_ns1 = 0;\r\n\t\t\tfor (int run = 0; run < 20000000 / size; run++) {\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\t\t\tAHashMap<Variant, Variant, VariantHasher, VariantComparator> dictionary;\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx ++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\t\t\tdictionary.insert(idx, idx);\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx ++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\t\t\tdictionary.insert(idx, idx);\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t2 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\ttime_ns += std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::nanoseconds>(t1 - t0).count();\r\n\t\t\t\ttime_ns1 += std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::nanoseconds>(t2 - t1).count();\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << \"insert:\" << size << std::endl;\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << time_ns / 1000 / 1000 << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << \"insert existing:\" << size << std::endl;\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << time_ns1 / 1000 / 1000 << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tsize_t time_ns = 0;\r\n\t\t\tfor (int run = 0; run < 20000000 / size; run++) {\r\n\t\t\t\tAHashMap<Variant, Variant, VariantHasher, VariantComparator> dictionary;\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx ++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\t\t\tdictionary.insert(idx, idx);\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx ++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\t\t\tdictionary.erase(idx);\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\t\t\ttime_ns += std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::nanoseconds>(t1 - t0).count();\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << \"erase:\" << size << std::endl;\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << time_ns / 1000 / 1000 << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tsize_t time_ns = 0;\r\n\t\t\tfor (int run = 0; run < 20000000 / size; run++) {\r\n\t\t\t\tAHashMap<Variant, Variant, VariantHasher, VariantComparator> dictionary;\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx ++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\t\t\tdictionary.insert(idx, idx);\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\tsize_t total = 0;\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx ++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\t\t\ttotal += dictionary.has(idx);\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\t\t\ttime_ns += std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::nanoseconds>(t1 - t0).count();\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t// Prevent compiling this out.\r\n\t\t\t\tvolatile_size_t = total;\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << \"get:\" << size << std::endl;\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << time_ns / 1000 / 1000 << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nI tested 3 key-value pairs, across a few different sizes:\r\n\r\n- **<int16_t, int16_t>** (claimed by @Nazarwadim to favour `OAHashMap`, but [without tests](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/92554#issuecomment-22073810040))\r\n- **<int64_t, int64_t>**\r\n- **<Variant, Variant>**\r\n\r\nAnd there's the raw results, for anyone interested:\r\n- [AHashMap.Variant.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20533750/AHashMap.Variant.txt)\r\n- [OAHashMap.int16_t.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20533751/OAHashMap.int16_t.txt)\r\n- [OAHashMap.int64_t.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20533752/OAHashMap.int64_t.txt)\r\n- [OAHashMap.Variant.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20533753/OAHashMap.Variant.txt)\r\n- [AHashMap.int16_t.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20533748/AHashMap.int16_t.txt)\r\n- [AHashMap.int64_t.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20533749/AHashMap.int64_t.txt)\r\n\r\nWe're approaching quite a few numbers now, so I made them into graphs of size vs time spent (lower is better):\r\n\r\n![get](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8d5265ef-4b92-42dd-b97d-7bb5c16250ad)\r\n\r\n![insert](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7492e535-06ff-4635-a548-e2b1015e6922)\r\n\r\n![update](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f3101814-3a06-4372-b87e-740b58c6b88c)\r\n\r\n![erase](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0181708c-e92f-46d5-b12d-7d72d426c0ba)\r\n\r\nI think it's clear that `AHashMap` should be a net improvement in nearly all situations, without much risk of regression.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1349613124,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzQ5NjEzMTI0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/for%20pr%20meeting","name":"for pr meeting","description":"","color":"88f795","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/22","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22/labels","number":22,"state":"closed","title":"4.5","description":"","creator":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauermann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/subscriptions","organizatio